From 1b00e9bdd36bb3f3aa56aa6720310093de762b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:24:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fuse Swish/SiLU into Convolution (activation_type 7) and
 recover x*sigmoid(x) patterns in ncnnoptimize

YOLO-family models (SiLU everywhere) currently keep one Swish layer per
convolution on every backend, and onnx2ncnn only recognises x*sigmoid(x) when
the convolution output has a single consumer, so a quarter of the SiLUs survive
as Split + Sigmoid + BinaryOp(MUL) (three dispatches and two barriers on Vulkan).

* activation_type 7 = swish (x * sigmoid(x)) in fused_activation.h (scalar and
  the create_activation_layer fallback -> Swish layer), in the arm/x86/loongarch/
  mips/riscv vector activation helpers (all of which already had swish/sigmoid
  helpers) and in vulkan_activation.comp.
* ncnnoptimize: new pass fuse_split_sigmoid_mul_swish() turns
  x -> Split -> {a, b}; Sigmoid(b); Mul(a, sigmoid) into Swish(x), and the
  Convolution / ConvolutionDepthWise / InnerProduct activation fusions accept
  Swish (-> activation_type 7).

YOLOv9-t 320 (fox-person-cat, 655 layers): the optimised graph shrinks to 388
layers (179 convolutions carry 9=7, 44 Split+Sigmoid+Mul triples removed).
On an Apple M1 (Mesa Honeykrisp Vulkan) that is 978 -> ~740 dispatches and
~2020 -> ~1680 barriers per inference; Vulkan fp16 29.0 -> 25.2 ms and fp32
33.8 -> 30.2 ms in the same (noisy) pass. Output is unchanged within fp16
rounding: fp32 Vulkan max|diff| vs onnxruntime 0.0016 (0.0021 before), fp32
NEON CPU 0.0015; fp16 differs from the unfused fp16 graph by the rounding of
the fused epilogue only.

